Make vtkPythonUtil::AddModule safe in a static build, and give it its hook.

Every wrapped module's init calls vtkPythonUtil::AddModule, which calls
vtkmodules.on_vtk_module_init(name), the pending list behind the @override
helpers. AddModule checks nothing: PyImport_ImportModule, PyObject_GetAttrString
and PyObject_CallObject may each return NULL, and it calls through and
Py_DECREFs them all regardless.

In a static build that is what happens. `import vtkmodules` runs
_load_vtkmodules_static() near the top of __init__.py, which imports
_vtkmodules_static and so runs every module's init, while __init__.py has not
yet reached its definition of on_vtk_module_init further down. Each AddModule
then gets a NULL hook, and:
  * PyObject_CallObject(NULL, ...) formats "'%s' object is not callable" from
    the type of NULL, reading wild memory (the garbage type names);
  * Py_DECREF(execVal) and Py_DECREF(pFunc) on NULL decrement the word at
    address 0;
  * the TypeError is left set, and CPython reports it later from wherever the
    collector runs ("Exception ignored in garbage collection ... in
    _lock_unlock_module").
Seen in libcvc's CPython-wasm host (pycvc_host), which embeds the static wasm
vtk-python: a -sSAFE_HEAP=1 link segfaults in AddModule under
PyInit__vtkmodules_static -> PyInit_vtkCommonCore, and an -sASSERTIONS link
aborts at exit on the overwritten address 0. Upstream VTK master (9.7.2) still
has both the ordering and the unchecked calls.

Two changes, each enough on its own (verified both ways in that host):
  * vtkPythonUtil.cxx: AddModule checks each step, uses Py_XDECREF, and clears
    a failure: the hook is advisory, and an error left set by a module's init
    surfaces somewhere unrelated.
  * vtkmodules/__init__.py.in: the static components load at the end of the
    file, after the hooks they call are defined.

No change for shared builds beyond the checks: there the placeholder expands to
a comment, wherever it sits.
--- a/Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/__init__.py.in
+++ b/Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/__init__.py.in
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@ def _load_vtkmodules_static():
     if 'vtkmodules_vtkCommonCore' not in sys.builtin_module_names:
         import _vtkmodules_static
 
-@_vtkmodules_static_import@
+# cvcpkg: called at the end of this file, once the hooks below exist.
 
 
 #------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -154,3 +154,9 @@ def on_vtk_module_init_completed():
         LOADED_MODULES.add(module_name)
         for import_name in MODULE_MAPPER.get(module_name, []):
             importlib.import_module(import_name)
+
+
+#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# cvcpkg: load the static components last. Loading them runs every wrapped module's
+# init, and each calls on_vtk_module_init (vtkPythonUtil::AddModule), so it must exist.
+@_vtkmodules_static_import@
--- a/Wrapping/PythonCore/vtkPythonUtil.cxx
+++ b/Wrapping/PythonCore/vtkPythonUtil.cxx
@@ -1043,15 +1043,27 @@ void vtkPythonUtil::AddModule(const char* name)
   vtkPythonMap->ModuleList->push_back(name);
 
   // Register module name into pending list for deferred side module loading
+  // cvcpkg: check each step. A static build runs every module's init while vtkmodules is still
+  // executing (_load_vtkmodules_static), and the hook may not exist yet; a NULL pFunc then reached
+  // PyObject_CallObject and the Py_DECREFs (writes through address 0) and left the error set.
+  // The hook is advisory, so a failure is cleared rather than reported from the module's init.
   PyObject* pModule = PyImport_ImportModule("vtkmodules");
-  PyObject* pFunc = PyObject_GetAttrString(pModule, "on_vtk_module_init");
-  PyObject* pArgs = PyTuple_New(1);
-  PyTuple_SetItem(pArgs, 0, PyUnicode_FromString(name));
-  PyObject* execVal = PyObject_CallObject(pFunc, pArgs);
-  Py_DECREF(execVal);
-  Py_DECREF(pArgs);
-  Py_DECREF(pFunc);
-  Py_DECREF(pModule);
+  PyObject* pFunc = pModule ? PyObject_GetAttrString(pModule, "on_vtk_module_init") : nullptr;
+  PyObject* execVal = nullptr;
+  if (pFunc)
+  {
+    PyObject* pArgs = PyTuple_New(1);
+    PyTuple_SetItem(pArgs, 0, PyUnicode_FromString(name));
+    execVal = PyObject_CallObject(pFunc, pArgs);
+    Py_DECREF(pArgs);
+  }
+  if (!execVal)
+  {
+    PyErr_Clear();
+  }
+  Py_XDECREF(execVal);
+  Py_XDECREF(pFunc);
+  Py_XDECREF(pModule);
 }
 
 //------------------------------------------------------------------------------
